        "title": "Preserve user-interrupted message in SDK run state after Esc",
        "summary": "The agent runtime extracts the hardcoded user-interrupted message into a new `USER_INTERRUPTED_MESSAGE` constant, which the SDK re-exports to allow external consumption. A new SDK function, `toUserInterruptedRunState`, inspects a `RunState` and swaps the SDK's generic cancellation text for `USER_INTERRUPTED_MESSAGE` when resuming an interrupted turn. The CLI incorporates this by calling `toUserInterruptedRunState` in its abort handler and post-run persistence path, ensuring the next prompt in the same chat resumes from a history that explicitly records the user stopped the agent, rather than a generic \"session ended\" state. Three test cases verify that this prevents the model from receiving contradictory context when the user hits Esc and types a follow-up prompt.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "In `packages/agent-runtime/src/util/messages.ts`, the string \"User interrupted the response...\" is extracted into `USER_INTERRUPTED_MESSAGE`. In `sdk/src/run.ts`, a new exported function `toUserInterruptedRunState` swaps an SDK's generic cancellation message for `USER_INTERRUPTED_MESSAGE` in the session state. In `cli/src/hooks/use-send-message.ts`, the abort handler and post-run persistence logic now call `toUserInterruptedRunState` to ensure the interrupted turn's history ends with the user-interrupted message.",
