        "calls": 1,
        "text": "When you press the escape key to stop an AI coding task, the system now records that you personally stopped it, rather than treating it as a general session shutdown. This matters to anyone using the free terminal assistant: if you immediately type a follow-up instruction, the AI understands you paused the previous work and remembers what you were doing, so it does not get confused by contradictory context. Previously, a quick stop-and-continue could leave the AI thinking the session had crashed or ended naturally, leading to awkward restarts.",
